<header><p class="st-kicker">princely state · Indian princely states</p><h1 class="st-title">Savanur State</h1><p class="st-meta">1680 CE – 1948 CE (approx.) · capital Savanur</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">A small Muslim-ruled state in northern Karnataka, held by a Pathan family of Nawabs granted their lands under Aurangzeb.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>Savanur was founded around 1680 when <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/abdul-rauf-khan">Abdul Rauf Khan</a>, an Afghan (Miana) officer, received a grant from the Mughal emperor <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/aurangzeb">Aurangzeb</a> in the Carnatic. His descendants ruled as Nawabs of Savanur.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>The Nawabs ruled a territory of black-soil <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cotton">cotton</a> and grain country between <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dharwad">Dharwad</a> and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tungabhadra-river">Tungabhadra</a>. They lost much land to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/maratha-empire">Marathas</a> and to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hyder-ali">Hyder Ali</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tipu-sultan">Tipu Sultan of Mysore</a> in the 18th century, and came under British protection after 1818 in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/southern-maratha-country">Southern Maratha Country</a>.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>Savanur acceded to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/india">India</a> and merged into <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/bombay-presidency">Bombay Province</a> in 1948, passing to <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/mysore-state">Mysore State</a> (now <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/karnataka">Karnataka</a>) in 1956. The town lies in Haveri district.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/savanur-state.jpg" alt="Savanur State" width="320" height="178"><figcaption>Image: Great Britain India Office · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Sangli-Jamkhandi_map.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1680 CE – 1948 CE (approx.)</dd><dt>Centuries</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/17th-century">17th century</a> – <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>princely state</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>feudal</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Savanur</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Abdul Rauf Khan</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Islam, Hinduism</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Kannada, Urdu</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/india">India</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Savanur</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1814&amp;focus=savanur-state" aria-label="Savanur State on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="6739 1621 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Savanur State lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M7059 1877L7364 1601M7059 1877L7364 1602M7059 1877L7018 1386"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M7364 1601h0M7364 1602h0M7018 1386h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M7059 1877h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M7059 1877h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks its recorded location. <a href="/atlas?year=1814&amp;focus=savanur-state">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>
